        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $x$ in terms of $a$ and $b$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\sqrt{ab}$.\n\nApply Pythagoras to the two smaller triangles and the whole triangle.",
          "worked": "By Pythagoras, the squares of the two shorter sides of the whole triangle are $x^2+a^2$ and $x^2+b^2$. Applying Pythagoras to the whole triangle:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^2+a^2)+(x^2+b^2)&=(a+b)^2\\\\2x^2+a^2+b^2&=a^2+2ab+b^2\\\\2x^2&=2ab\\\\x^2&=ab\\\\x&=\\sqrt{ab}.\\end{align*}$$\nTake the positive square root because $x$ is a length.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
