            "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 14 p14-q13-diagram2\"}\n\\usetikzlibrary{calc,angles}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (B) at (5,0);\n\\coordinate (C) at (4,2);\n\\coordinate (H) at (4,0);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (B) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=2.5cm];\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (A)--(C)--(B)--cycle (C)--(H);\n\\pic[draw=black,line width=0.4pt,angle radius=3mm] {right angle=A--C--B};\n\\pic[draw=black,line width=0.4pt,angle radius=3mm] {right angle=C--H--A};\n\\path (A)--(H) node[midway,below] {$a$};\n\\path (H)--(B) node[midway,below] {$b$};\n\\path (H)--(C) node[midway,left] {$x$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
            "src": null,
            "widthMm": 55,
            "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
            "overlayOf": null,
            "transparent": false,
            "axes": null,
            "spec": {
              "sourcePage": 14,
              "sourceRegion": "Question 13(b), semicircle in the right column",
              "description": "The same triangle inscribed in an upper semicircle with the hypotenuse as diameter. Decorative cyan fill omitted.",
              "mathematics": "Diameter a+b, altitude x, hypotenuse segments a and b, upper vertex on the semicircle, and both right angles retained.",
              "answerVisibility": "No radius value or inequality proof is supplied in the question figure."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{a+b}{2}\\geq\\sqrt{ab}$.\n\nThe altitude $x=\\sqrt{ab}$ cannot exceed the semicircle's radius.",
          "worked": "The semicircle has diameter $a+b$, so its radius is $\\dfrac{a+b}{2}$. The vertical height of any point on the semicircle above its diameter cannot exceed this radius. Therefore,\n$$x\\leq\\frac{a+b}{2}.$$\nUsing $x=\\sqrt{ab}$ from part (a),\n$$\\frac{a+b}{2}\\geq\\sqrt{ab}$$\nfor all positive $a$ and $b$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      }
